Fix ONLY the lost-update defect in src/metrics.mjs. Independent of the pipeline.mjs fixes in
source, but this card is chained after them because every card in this repair writes the same
repair/manifest.json, and a card with no dependsOn edge cannot see a sibling's manifest additions.

Current (defective) code in src/metrics.mjs:
```
export async function record(metrics, key, deps = {}) {
	const io = deps.io ?? immediateIo;
	const current = metrics.counts.get(key) ?? 0;
	await io.yield();
	metrics.counts.set(key, current + 1);
}
```
Replace with:
```
export async function record(metrics, key, deps = {}) {
	const io = deps.io ?? immediateIo;
	await io.yield();
	const current = metrics.counts.get(key) ?? 0;
	metrics.counts.set(key, current + 1);
}
```
Reading `current` AFTER the io turn instead of before is the entire fix: every increment must survive, including
when several callers hold the same metrics object at once. Do not touch src/pipeline.mjs.

Verified empirically in a scratch copy: on top of both pipeline.mjs fixes, this change flips the remaining two
frozen scenarios to green: `concurrent-records-of-one-key-do-not-lose-updates`,
`interleaved-records-across-keys-stay-exact` — all 6 scenarios this fixture defines are then green.

